      "overall_structure": {
        "value": "Duplex (α-ferrite + austenite) microstructure. After solution treatment at 800 °C for 1 h the M5C2-carbide phase disappeared and martensite reverse-transformed to austenite; a large amount of strip ferrite, termed α-ferrite (to distinguish it from δ-ferrite formed at high temperature), was observed, together with austenite islands in the δ-ferrite/α-ferrite ground."
